// Source: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dax/startat-statement-dax
// Construct: Fewer START AT values than ORDER BY columns.
// Expect: parse
// Reference: rejects - START AT must supply exactly one value per ORDER BY column (2 expected, 1 given)
// Divergence: START AT value list
// Normalized: written from the documented rule: "There can be as many arguments in the START AT statement as there are in the ORDER BY statement, but not more."
EVALUATE
    'Customer'
ORDER BY
    'Customer'[Country] ASC,
    'Customer'[City] ASC
START AT "Germany"
